course: dictionary
lesson: 5995
title: Meanwhile
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Meanwhile» is a signal word. It tells you that something else is happening at the same time, or that the story is moving to another place. «Meanwhile, back at the castle...» means the writer is switching to what is happening there now.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Meanwhile Ruby, Mia's best friend since Reception, was squashed onto the arm of the sofa by six new kids.» The word meanwhile tells you this is happening at the same time as something else in the story. Try your meaning in the sentence: "at the same time" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Meanwhile can also mean the time while you wait for something. «That often passes; meanwhile Becca can give her space and find her own friends.» It can also compare two different things, like Sam and his sister in «Sam loves maths; meanwhile, his sister hates it.»
fact: Meanwhile is an adverb. In the phrase in the meanwhile, it works as a noun.
fact: «Meanwhile» means at the same time, while something else is happening.
fact: It can also mean in the time between two events, such as while you wait for a bus.
fact: It can show a contrast, comparing two different things or people.
fact: Writers use it to move from one place or character to another in a story.
exercise: «Meanwhile, back at the castle...» What does meanwhile tell the reader? | *Something else is happening at the same time | Someone else is lost in the woods | The story has ended
exercise: Sam loves maths; meanwhile, his sister hates it. What is meanwhile showing? | A place to sit | A time of day | The same thing said twice | *A contrast between two different things
exercise: The bus is late; ___, let's sit down on the bench. Which word fits the gap? | Although | Because | Yesterday | *Meanwhile
test: The cat slept on the mat; ___, the dog chased a ball in the garden. Which word fits best? | *Meanwhile | Tomorrow | Under | Because
test: «Meanwhile, monks in the West copied old books by hand and kept learning alive.» What does meanwhile mean here? | *At the same time, while other things were happening | Inside a book | Before the books were written | Very quickly
exam: Which meaning fits «Meanwhile Ruby... was squashed onto the arm of the sofa by six new kids»? | Feeling cross about the sofa | Far away in another country | A short time before dinner | *At the same time, while something else is happening
